# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Offer a spell whose only legal targets need X above zero, then announce X before choosing targets.
# Forcing: Every opposing nonland permanent has mana value 2, so Repeal has no legal target until X is 2.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no instants and no untapped mana, so Repeal resolves unanswered.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Repeal is offered, X=2 is announced, Grizzly Bears returns to its owner's hand, and a card is drawn.
#   LOSE = Repeal is not offered, or X=2 does not make Grizzly Bears a legal target.
#   TIMEOUT = the cast stalls between the X announcement and target selection.
# Card roles:
#   Repeal — targets a nonland permanent with mana value X and draws a card.
#   Island — three sources pay exactly {2}{U}.
#   Grizzly Bears and Mind Stone — mana value 2 targets; no permanent has mana value 0.
#   Island and Mountain libraries — keep both draws legal.
# Protocol path: cast action, NumericInputReq, NumericInputResp, target selection, mana payment, and resolution.

[metadata]
Name:X-Dependent Target
Goal:Survive
Turns:1
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Cast Repeal with X=2 to return Grizzly Bears.

